  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Social and Economic Inclusion Opportunities for Displaced People Fleeing Ukraine to Hungary</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As the war in Ukraine entered its second year on 24 February 2023, more than four million border crossings to Hungary have been registered, both through the Ukrainian and Romanian borders. As the conflict is getting protracted and about 42% of the respondents plan to remain in Hungary (IOM DTM), transitioning from the provision of immediate life-saving assistance to comprehensive and multidimensional social inclusion measures is essential to facilitate their successful integration into the Hungarian society.  Recognizing the challenges faced by refugees and the fact that post-migration stressors can be equally or even more negatively impactful than pre-migration trauma regarding refugees&#x2019; mental health, their ability to recover from past traumas and to adjust to their new environment, the project adopts a holistic and strength-based approach. This relies on a comprehensive integration package contributing to upholding refugees&#x2019; well-being and facilitating their successful integration within the host society. Therefore, the project will facilitate the socio-economic inclusion of refugees beyond the timeline of the project while promoting solidarity and social cohesion within the host community. As a result, refugees will have improved capacity and knowledge to navigate their way through the society and establish themselves as a part of it.</narrative>
  </description>
